+#### 4 Nov W1 supplementary enhancement — feature pairs and surrogate comparison (proposed; NOT historical freeze evidence)
+
+**Reason for additional validation-only investigation:** The original one-case SHAP check and single-feature reports cannot establish whether important *combinations* of academic progress, participation and financial-status features create non-additive model responses. The new work investigates **the five leading semantic groups per case and their ten unordered pairs**, then compares linear local surrogate fidelity with and without pair terms and penalties. Pair masking is a descriptive model-response experiment, not formal SHAP interactions or causation. This **does not rescind** the 2 Nov amendment, authorize a final-test rerun, replace TabICL, or reopen the scientific protocol.
+
+**New location (no edits to Yolanda's original runner):** `W1_Noey_Enhanced/`; keep code, tests, proposed explanation and handoff separate. Case-level evidence is generated under `W1_Noey_Enhanced/outputs/` on a restricted analysis machine; do not commit student-level case files or any private model/checkpoint.
+
+| ID | Revised Noey task | Method and check | Evidence/status |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| W1.1 | Case selection + **local/grouped SHAP** | The frozen TabICL configuration on existing train/validation split; all 544 validation cases, retaining every row and source ID; no case sampling; save signed grouped SHAP, reference values and top-five groups | **Code prepared; genuine 544-case run pending.** Original one-case smoke check is not equivalent |
+| W1.2 | Feature influence, **pairs** and faithfulness | Summarise mean absolute SHAP across all 544 validation cases; ranked-top-five vs 50 random deletion orders. For each case test 10 top-five group pairs: `p(mask AB) - p(mask A) - p(mask B) + p(original)`; distinguish this reference-masking nonadditivity from formal SHAP interactions. Compare **OLS, Ridge, Lasso × main-only / main+pair** on 32 frozen-TabICL masking outcomes per case, train on 24 and report MAE on eight held-out higher-order masks; nested CV tuning on train only | **Code and synthetic tests prepared; real SHAP/pair/surrogate metrics pending.** Never infer global or causal importance from explanations |
+| W1.3 | Robustness | Ten distinct seeds and ten training-background samples per case; up to ten eligible, range-clipped grade perturbations with model score shift ≤0.01; compare top-five overlap, rank Spearman, pair-rank agreement and insufficient accepted perturbations | **Execution pending**; 0.80 is a heuristic warning, not an explanation certification |
+| W1.4 | Multi-feature model recourse and possible support | For all 544 validation students, export individual and combined grade (+3/20), approved-unit (+2), overdue tuition and debtor-status input simulations with original/revised TabICL probability, percentage-point change and cohort rank. For **all flagged students**, test single/joint administrative debt and tuition-status resolution for capacity-policy recourse; distinguish historical-grade sensitivity from feasible support targets. Do not infer intervention effectiveness | **Execution pending**; no real-world counterfactual or intervention efficacy claims |
+| W1.5 | Findings, limitations, team review | Report numeric outcomes, uncertainty, stability by mode, pair nonadditivity, all six surrogate fidelity/complexity comparisons, recourse/no-recourse and limits; different reviewer signs off before adding to final report | **Findings template and Yolanda handoff prepared; actual results and review pending** |
+
+**Surrogate choice rule:** Lower held-out masking-pattern MAE means better *local mimicry of TabICL* on those tested masks. Report sparsity and out-of-range predictions too. Ridge/Lasso do **not** change the underlying TabICL model or its frozen final-test predictions. The added investigation is explicitly **post-final-test supplementary validation work**, so it cannot be claimed as a pre-freeze acceptance gate.
+
+**Mandatory handoff:** `W1_Noey_Enhanced/docs/HANDOFF_TO_YOLANDA.md`. If the W1 enhanced audit exposes weak/stable explanations or an apparent non-additive pattern, **update claims/limitations only**—this alone is not justification for rerunning the final test. Any verified defect in the prior final-test methodology must be escalated with independent review, lock preservation and explicit authorization; never silently repeat a once-only evaluation.
